# Example MCP client config (Streamable HTTP)

This server speaks MCP over Streamable HTTP, not stdio — the same URL works
whether the client is on the same machine as the server or elsewhere on the
LAN. Point any MCP client that supports an HTTP/URL server entry at:

```
http://<host>:8420/mcp
```

`<host>` is `localhost` when the client runs on the same machine as the
indexer/server, or the Mac Mini's LAN hostname/IP (e.g. `host.example.invalid`
or `192.0.2.10`) otherwise.

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "resmed-data": {
      "url": "http://host.example.invalid:8420/mcp",
      "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer <local-keychain-token>" }
    }
  }
}
```

Every HTTP request requires the local Keychain bearer token. Retrieve it explicitly with `resmed-data-mcp http-token`, and set the client Authorization header locally. Never put the real value in Git or Notion. Keep the server on the home LAN; do not expose port 8420 to the internet.
